{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1513384-question-about-db-charm-themes","id":1513384,"title":"Question about DB Charm themes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-31T06:06:16-07:00","id":1513384,"title":"Question about DB Charm themes","content":"Do third edition Dragon-Blooded have any particular Charms that allow them to empower/stand in solidarity with other soldiers, particularly mortals? If not, does that seem like valid design space for the Exalted who exist to make up for in numbers what they lack in personal power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T11:14:35-07:00","id":1513426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1513384-question-about-db-charm-themes#post1513384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do third edition Dragon-Blooded have any particular Charms that allow them to empower/stand in solidarity with other soldiers, particularly mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean in a way other than leading with the War Ability?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not, does that seem like valid design space for the Exalted who exist to make up for in numbers what they lack in personal power?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though in practical terms that's really more of a conceit on a setting level than a personal one.<br /> <br /> I'm giving the Charms a quick overview, but I can't see anything that quite empowers other people in the manner of bestowing powers on them (although possibly there's something in there that can provide some dice enhancements). I think that may be the kind of thing this Edition can effectively differentiate Terrestrial from Celestial Exalted with.<br /> <br /> They do have things to stand in solidarity insofar as there are Charms under the likes of Integrity to reinforce certain Intimacies in certain ways. If you've got a Major Tie of loyalty to an army, there are things that can help with that.<br /> <br /> Again, besides the War Charms. Some decent ways to power up battle groups in there.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T18:51:27-07:00","id":1513591,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Isator Levi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-04T13:44:58-07:00","id":1513890,"title":"","content":"I think they might have more Charms playing off of the Sworn Kinship specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T13:07:44-07:00","id":1514602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1513384-question-about-db-charm-themes#post1513384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do third edition Dragon-Blooded have any particular Charms that allow them to empower/stand in solidarity with other soldiers, particularly mortals? If not, does that seem like valid design space for the Exalted who exist to make up for in numbers what they lack in personal power?</div> </div> </div> </div>In second edition, this was a big theme for Dragon-Blooded, conspicuous in its absence for 3E.<br /> <br /> I think that it's valid charm space to play with, regardless.<br /> <br /> But I'd remind you to be careful of game balance.<br /> <br /> For example.<br /> <br /> You said, specifically, &quot;soldiers&quot;. So let's look at soldiers.<br /> <br /> A battle ready soldier's best attack is 7 dice. Not very much.<br /> Their defense is 4.<br /> <br /> Two dragons of infantry is 12 dice. Against everything touching the battlegroup.<br /> With elite drill their defense is 6.<br /> <br /> Throw on a Command backed by Tactics Mean Everything (coming from your legendary Dragon-Blooded commander) and a regular 2 dice stunt and that attack goes up to 23 dice. 25 dice if the battlegroup also stunts.<br /> <br /> Throw on Roaring Dragon Officer and Flame Warden Stance, and their defense goes up to 13 (15 with stunts). Scene long.<br /> <br /> And that's 4 Charms.<br /> <br /> Three or four 25 dice attacks on Parry ~14 each round.<br /> <br /> Wanna make them Elite Troops? That's 29 dice attacks on Parry 17.<br /> <br /> (A 5/5/1 Solar with a daiklave, stunt, and full Excellency is throwing 28 dice against 1 target. Fear the battlegroup.)<br /> <br /> Then charms like Blazing Courageous Swordsman Inspiration, Deadly Wildfire Legion, and Blessed Dragon Champion push these numbers even higher.<br /> <br /> Forget the Dragon-Blooded, for a moment:<br /> <br /> Take elite troops, give them a mortal commander with War 3 Charisma 3, let them stunt and they are throwing out 16 dice attacks.<br /> <br /> A t-rex throws 15 dice with a stunt.<br /> <br /> My point is, the existing rules for buffing combatants in an army are powerful. You absolutely can make your own charms for buffing mortals, but consider what the interplay is going to be.<br /> <br /> You want something that works within the current system. In 2E Dragon-Blooded could increase a mortal's Melee score from 3 to 5 with a stater charm. This would be a very bad idea in 3E. As would, say, giving mortals reroll 6s.<br /> <br /> Good ideas would be stuff that doesn't raise the cap. For example:<br /> <br /> Increase the Size of the unit to the Dragon-Blooded's (Essence)<br /> Raise their stats from Conscripts to Battleready Troops for the scene.<br /> Raise their stats from Battleready to Elite for a round.<br /> Increase Drill for a scene.<br /> Increase Drill permanently after a period of training.<br /> Confer Hardness 1 on the troops so they are immune to Anima Flux<br /> Enhancements not directly related to combat (weathering environmental hazards, increased mobility, and the like).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 06-12-2023, 05:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}